Local patch to jtp10181 "Zooz ZSE44 Temperature Humidity XS Sensor" v1.2.0
(Drivers/zooz/zooz-zse44-temp-humidity.groovy), installed on the hub as driver 789.
Re-apply after any HPM/driver update until fixed upstream.

1. getParamStoredMap() used evaluate() to read the configVals data value. The hub
   sandbox now rejects it ("Unrestricted script compilation is not allowed"), so any
   driver reload or hub reboot wiped every sensor's stored parameter values and
   forced a full re-send on the next wake-up. Replaced with a plain parser.
2. Firmware 2.40 (Guest Bathroom sensor) answers 200 when parameter #15 (hardware
   humidity offset) is set to 100 (no offset); its readings show no +10% offset
   (it tracks the 2.00-firmware master sensor within a few points). Treat that
   answer as in sync instead of retrying on every wake-up.

--- a/Drivers/zooz/zooz-zse44-temp-humidity.groovy
+++ b/Drivers/zooz/zooz-zse44-temp-humidity.groovy
@@ -462,7 +462,7 @@
 		Integer paramVal = getParamValueAdj(param)
 		Integer storedVal = getParamStoredValue(param.num)
 
-		if ((paramVal != null) && (state.resyncAll || (storedVal != paramVal))) {
+		if ((paramVal != null) && (state.resyncAll || !paramInSync(param, paramVal, storedVal))) {
 			logDebug "Changing ${param.name} - ${param.title} (#${param.num}) from ${storedVal} to ${paramVal}"
 			cmds += configSetGetCmd(param, paramVal)
 		}
@@ -516,6 +516,14 @@
 //These have to be added in after the fact or groovy complains
 void fixParamsMap() {
 	paramsMap['settings'] = [fixed: true]
+}
+
+//Local patch (djkoser): firmware 2.40 answers 200 when parameter #15 (humidity offset) is set
+//to 100 (no offset), and its readings show no +10% offset. Treat that answer as in sync instead
+//of re-sending the parameter on every wake-up.
+boolean paramInSync(Map param, Integer paramVal, Integer storedVal) {
+	if (storedVal == paramVal) return true
+	return (param.name == "humidOffsetHw" && firmwareVersion >= 2.40 && paramVal == 100 && storedVal == 200)
 }
 
 Integer getParamValueAdj(Map param) {
@@ -801,13 +809,24 @@
 	//device.updateDataValue("configVals", configsMap.inspect())
 }
 
+//Local patch (djkoser): the hub sandbox now rejects evaluate() ("Unrestricted script compilation
+//is not allowed"), which wiped configVals whenever the driver reloaded. Parse "[2:10, 3:20]" directly.
+Map parseConfigVals(String str) {
+	TreeMap map = [:]
+	str?.replaceAll(/[\[\]\s]/, "")?.split(",")?.each { String kv ->
+		List p = kv.split(":") as List
+		if (p.size() == 2 && p[0].isInteger() && p[1].isInteger()) map[p[0] as Integer] = p[1] as Integer
+	}
+	return map
+}
+
